  "number": "2.1.65",
  "title": "",
  "body": "     Converting terminating decimal to fraction form    <p>Convert the termination decimal \\({@val_decim@}\\) to fraction form.<\/p> <p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]<\/p>    <h3>Worked solution<\/h3> <p>Step 1: Identify the whole number and decimal parts.<\/p> <p>The whole number part is {@whole_part@}. <\/p> <p>The decimal part is {@decimal_part@}. <\/p> <p>Step 2: Convert the decimal part to a fraction and simplify it by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by the GCD. {@decimal_part_frac@}<\/p> <p>Step 3: Combine the whole number and the fraction to get \\({@ta@}\\) .<\/p>   1  0.1  0    2023060500    aa: rand_with_step(27,399,5); bb: rand_with_step(257,399,3); val1_aa: aa\/10; val2_aa: aa\/100; val3_aa: aa\/1000; val1_bb: bb\/10; val2_bb: bb\/100; val3_bb: bb\/1000; val_decim: float(rand([val1_aa,val2_aa,val3_aa,val1_bb,val2_bb,val3_bb])); whole_part:floor(val_decim); decimal_part:val_decim-whole_part; decimal_part_frac:rat(decimal_part) ta: if val_decim=float(val1_aa) then val1_aa else (if val_decim=float(val2_aa) then val2_aa else (if val_decim=float(val3_aa) then val3_aa else (if val_decim=float(val1_bb) then val1_bb else (if val_decim=float(val2_bb) then val2_bb else val3_bb))));       <p>Terminating decimal: \\({@val_decim@}\\)<\/p> <p>fraction form: \\({@ta@}\\)<\/p> <p>To express \\({@val_decim@}\\) as a fraction:<\/p> <p>The whole number part is \\({@whole_part@}\\).<\/p. <p>The decimal part, \\({@decimal_part@}\\), can be written as \\({@decimal_part_frac@}\\).<\/p> <P>Combine the whole number \\({@whole_part@}\\) and the fraction \\({@decimal_part_frac@}\\)to get \\({@ta@}\\) .<\/p>      1  0  0   <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:green;\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"><\/i><\/span> Correct answer, well done.    <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:orange;\"><i class=\"fa fa-adjust\"><\/i><\/span> Your answer is partially correct.    <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:red;\"><i class=\"fa fa-times\"><\/i><\/span> Incorrect answer.   .  *10  none  1  i  cos-1  lang  [  0    ans1  algebraic  ta  5  1  0   0    1  0  0  1  3     prt1  1.0000000  1  1      0   AlgEquiv  ans1  ta   0  =  1   -1  prt1-1-T     =  0   -1  prt1-1-F       369126791  1932363033  1437358640  680567859  766989064  1787379254  2074718722  445831357  2110529022  1304783736  801936695  1941460124  636840516  1123217547  1640277215  333626499  731699463  386909988  685370035  1896746435  1294165834  1878492766  33055171  88405955  571514733  80909005  1488905233  17767562  454202225   1    ans1  ta    prt1  1.0000000  0.0000000  prt1-1-T        Add review   "
