  "title": "",
  "body": "     Simplification of rational expressions in partial fractions: 1.8 a,c    <p>Write the rational expression below as a sum of its partial fractions.<\/p> <p>\\(\\qquad \\displaystyle {@question_expression2@}=\\) [[input:ans3]] \\(+\\) [[input:ans4]] \\(+\\) [[input:ans5]] <\/p><p>\\(\\hspace{6cm} \\) [[validation:ans3]]\\(\\hspace{1.5cm} \\) [[validation:ans4]] \\(\\hspace{1.5cm} \\) [[validation:ans5]]<\/p> <p>\\(\\quad \\) [[feedback:prt2]]<\/p>    <p style=\"\">To write \\( \\displaystyle {@question_expression2@}\\) as a sum of its partial fractions we need to follow the steps below:<\/p> <p style=\"\">\\[{@question_expression2@} ={@part_frac_Aa@}+{@part_frac_Bb@}+{@part_frac_Cc@}\\]<\/p> <p style=\"\">Setting the numerators equal gives:<\/p> <p style=\"\">\\[{@expra@}\\]<\/p> <p style=\"\">Getting the coefficients \\(A\\) and \\(B\\), we have<\/p> <p style=\"\">Let \\(x=0:\\quad {@expr1a@} \\implies {@expAa@}\\). <\/p> <p style=\"\">Let \\(x={@-const_3@}:\\quad {@expr2b@} \\implies {@expCc@}\\).<\/p> <p style=\"\">Let \\(x={@(-const_2\/const_1)@}:\\quad {@expr3bc@} \\implies {@expBb@}\\).<\/p> <p style=\"\">The partial fraction is then,<\/p> <p style=\"\">\\[{@expr3c@}\\]<\/p>   1  0.1  0    2023060500    \/*...........Question 2.......................................*\/ \/*Defining the question*\/ const_1:1+rand(5);\/*The first constant coefficient*\/ const_2:1+rand(5);\/*The second constant*\/ const_3:1+rand(4);\/*The third constant*\/ const_4:1+rand(8);\/*The fourth constant*\/ zz1:rand_with_prohib(-7,7,[0]);\/* numerator_1*\/ zz2:rand_with_prohib(-7,7,[0]);\/* numerator_2*\/ zz3:rand_with_prohib(-7,7,[0]);\/* numerator_2*\/ part_frac_1a:zz1\/x;\/*The first Partial fraction*\/ part_frac_2b:zz2\/(const_1*x+const_2);\/*The second Partial fraction*\/ part_frac_3c:zz3\/(x+const_3);\/*The third Partial fraction*\/ question_expression2: factor(part_frac_1a+part_frac_2b+part_frac_3c); \/*model answer question 2*\/ ta1:part_frac_1a; ta2:part_frac_2b; ta3:part_frac_3c; ta4:ta1+ta2+ta3; ta1a: partfrac(question_expression2,x); \/*Worked solution codes for question 2 *\/ part_frac_Aa:A\/x; part_frac_Bb:B\/(const_1*x+const_2); part_frac_Cc:C\/(x+const_3); numerator_question_expression2:num(question_expression2); expra:A*(const_1*x+const_2)*(x+const_3)+B*x*(x+const_3)+C*x*(const_1*x+const_2)=numerator_question_expression2; \/*Find A, B and C*\/ expr1a:ev(expra,x=0); expAa:expr1a\/ev(((const_1*x+const_2)*(x+const_3)),x=0); expr2b:ev(expra,x=-const_3); expCc:expr2b\/ev((x*(const_1*x+const_2)),x=-const_3); coef_Bb:ev((-const_2\/const_1),simp); expr3bc:ev(expra,x=coef_Bb); expBb:expr3bc\/ev(x*(x+const_3),x=(-const_2\/const_1)); expr3c: question_expression2=ta1+ta2+ta3;       <br>\\(\\displaystyle {@question_expression2@} = {@ta1@}+{@ta2@}+{@ta3@}\\)      1  0  0   <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:green;\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"><\/i><\/span> Correct answer, well done.    <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:orange;\"><i class=\"fa fa-adjust\"><\/i><\/span> Your answer is partially correct.    <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:red;\"><i class=\"fa fa-times\"><\/i><\/span> Incorrect answer.   .  *10  dot  1  i  cos-1  lang  [  0    ans3  algebraic  ta1  5  1  0   0    1  0  0  1  3     ans4  algebraic  ta2  5  1  0   0    1  0  0  1  3     ans5  algebraic  ta3  5  1  0   0    1  0  0  1  3     prt2  1.0000000  1  1   \/*Node 1: Check answer is correct and in correct form*\/ sans_full: ans3+ans4+ans5; \/*Node 2: check if the answer is equivalent to the expression given*\/ \/*Node 3: Identify incorrect answers *\/ sans_set:{ans3,ans4,ans5}; ta_set:{ta1,ta2,ta3}; correct:intersect(sans_set,ta_set); incorrect:setdifference(sans_set,ta_set); any_correct: if 1<=cardinality(correct) and cardinality(correct)<=2 then 1 else 0;    0   EqualComAss  sans_full  ta4   0  =  1   -1  prt2-1-T     =  0   1  prt2-1-F       1   AlgEquiv  sans_full  ta4   0  +  0.5   -1  prt2-2-T   Your answer is equivalent to {@question_expression2@}. However, it is not written in full partial fractions.   -  0   2  prt2-2-F       2   AlgEquiv  any_correct  1   0  +  0.5   -1  prt2-3-T   <p>The following answer(s) is (are) correct: {@correct@}. However, the following answer(s) is (are) not correct: {@incorrect@}.<\/p><p>You can verify this by adding your answers together:<\/p><p>\\(\\displaystyle {@ans3@}+{@ans4@}+{@ans5@} = {@factor(sans_full)@} \\neq {@question_expression2@} \\).<\/p><br>   -  0   -1  prt2-3-F   <p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: left;\"><\/p><p>None of your answers are correct.<\/p><p>You can verify this by adding your answers together:<\/p><p>\\(\\displaystyle {@ans3@}+{@ans4@}+{@ans5@} = {@factor(sans_full)@} \\neq {@question_expression2@} \\).<\/p><br><br><p><\/p>     1683940633  814491475  1176498027  1791595496  2041012363  306975987  1367113354  881324740  67859650  540807275  319186946  749442268  750061270  1538443072  1660283107  1255863054  1362221502  285886768  731770444  234250700  1263730496  294954318  2090835825  2036175063  971220054  1257740261  1435185047  177316925  89132778  609837964  724817121  1521993290  1775421315  2000972727  1000697463  1946697759  1286814251  1902939745  2122642337  1870043618  877374424  1948555507  539560336  2086339096  1038384464  2050464077  2126613867  1096664441  823784154  1581146265  2019669899  418768918  242614903  457364220  1373399110  469283794  1448345549  1124487293  1804984798  1993542854  1366615310  1026629760  1782291860  1890385004  205678266  741682731   1    ans3  ta1    ans4  ta2    ans5  ta3    prt2  1.0000000  0.0000000  prt2-1-T     2    ans3  1    ans4  1    ans5  1    prt2  0.0000000  0.1000000  prt2-3-F        Add review   "
