  "id": "subsec-definition-of-a-circle-10",
  "level": "2",
  "url": "sec-circles.html#subsec-definition-of-a-circle-10",
  "type": "Checkpoint",
  "number": "4.2.4",
  "title": "",
  "body": "     Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Endpoints of a Diameter    <p>Find the center and radius of a circle with \\(A({@x_1@}, {@y_1@})\\) and \\(B({@x_2@}, {@y_2@})\\) as endpoints of its diameter.<\/p> <p> <b>Note:<\/b> Give your answer in \\(2\\) decimal places where necessary<\/p> <p> Centre \\(=\\) [[input:ans1]][[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]] <\/p> <p> Radius \\(=\\) [[input:ans2]] units [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]] <\/p> <p><\/p> <p>Note: For the centre coordinates, enter your values inside the parenthesis \\( \\left( a, b \\right) \\)<\/p>    <h3>Worked Solution<\/h3> <p>Let's apply these steps to the given endpoints \\(A({@x_1@},{@y_1@})\\) and \\(B({@x_2@},{@y_2@})\\):<\/p> <p><strong>Step 1:<\/strong> Find the midpoint (center) of the diameter \\( \\displaystyle M= \\left(\\frac{{x_1 + x_2}}{2}, \\frac{{y_1 + y_2}}{2}\\right)\\) <\/p> <p>\\(\\begin{align} \\text{Midpoint (M)} & = \\left(\\frac{{({@x_1@}) + ({@x_2@})}}{2}, \\frac{{({@y_1@}) + ({@y_2@})}}{2}\\right) \\\\ & = \\left(\\frac{{{@x_1+ x_2@}}}{2}, \\frac{{{@y_1+ y_2@}}}{2}\\right) \\\\ & = \\left({@(x_1+ x_2)\/2@},{@(y_1 + y_2)\/2@} \\right) \\end{align}\\)<\/p> <p><strong>Step 2:<\/strong> Find the distance (radius) from one of the endpoints to the center. <\/p> <p>The distance formula gives us the radius \\(R\\) as:<\/p> \\[R = \\sqrt{{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}}\\] <p>Here we can use the points \\(A({@x_1@},{@y_1@})\\) and center \\( C\\left({@(x_1+ x_2)\/2@},{@(y_1 + y_2)\/2@} \\right) \\) to find the radius \\(R\\). (Note: You can also use \\(B({@x_2@},{@y_2@})\\)): <\/p> <p>\\( \\displaystyle \\begin{align}\\text{Radius (R)} & =\\sqrt{{(({@x_2@}) - ({@(x_1+ x_2)\/2@}))^2 + (({@y_2@}) - ({@(y_1 + y_2)\/2@}))^2}} \\\\ & = \\sqrt{{({@x_2 - ((x_1+ x_2)\/2)@})^2 + ({@y_2 - ((y_1 + y_2)\/2)@})^2}} \\\\ & = \\sqrt{{@(x_2 - ((x_1+ x_2)\/2))^2 + (y_2 - ((y_1 + y_2)\/2))^2@}} \\\\ & = {@ratsimp(sqrt((x_2 - ((x_1+ x_2)\/2))^2 + (y_2 - ((y_1 + y_2)\/2))^2))@} \\end{align} \\)<\/p> <p>So, the radius of the circle is \\({@ratsimp(sqrt((x_2 - ((x_1+ x_2)\/2))^2 + (y_2 - ((y_1 + y_2)\/2))^2))@} \\) units<\/p> <p>Therefore, the center of the circle is \\( C [{@(x_1+ x_2)\/2@},{@(y_1 + y_2)\/2@} ] \\) and the radius is \\({@ratsimp(sqrt((x_2 - ((x_1+ x_2)\/2))^2 + (y_2 - ((y_1 + y_2)\/2))^2))@}\\) units.<\/p>   1  0.1  0    2023060500    \/*Question Variables*\/ x_1:rand_with_step(-5,5,1); \/*The value of x at endpoint A*\/ y_1:rand_with_step(-5,5,1); \/*The value of y at endpoint A*\/ x_2:rand_with_prohib(-5,5,[x_1]); \/*The value of x at endpoint B*\/ y_2:y_1; \/*The value of y at endpoint B*\/ ta1_1:(x_1+x_2)\/2; ta2_1:(y_1+y_2)\/2; ta1_2:decimalplaces((x_1+x_2)\/2,2); ta2_2:decimalplaces((y_1+y_2)\/2,2); ta1:[ta1_1,ta2_1]; ta1a:[ta1_2,ta2_2]; ta2:sqrt((ta1_1-x_1)^2+(ta2_1-y_1)^2); ta2a:decimalplaces(sqrt((ta1_1-x_1)^2+(ta2_1-y_1)^2),2);       <p>Finding the center and radius of a circle with \\(A({@x_1@}, {@y_1@})\\) and \\(B({@x_2@}, {@y_2@})\\) as endpoints of its diameter.<\/p> <p> Centre \\(={@ta1@}\\) <\/p> <p> Radius \\(={@ta2@}\\) <\/p>      1  0  0   <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:green;\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"><\/i><\/span> Correct answer, well done.    <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:orange;\"><i class=\"fa fa-adjust\"><\/i><\/span> Your answer is partially correct.    <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:red;\"><i class=\"fa fa-times\"><\/i><\/span> Incorrect answer.   .  *10  none  1  i  cos-1  lang  [  0    ans1  algebraic  ta1  6  1  0  [ ? , ?]  0    0  0  0  1  3     ans2  algebraic  ta2  4  1  0   0    0  0  0  1  3     prt1  1.0000000  1  1   \/*Node 1: Checks for the correct answer *\/ \/*Node 2: Mistake: Swapping the coordinates of the center point.*\/ mistake2: [ta2_1,ta1_1]; \/*Node 3: Checks for the correct answer in decimal form*\/    0   AlgEquiv  ans1  ta1   1  =  1   -1  prt1-1-T     =  0   2  prt1-1-F       1   AlgEquiv  ans1  mistake2   1  +  0   -1  prt1-2-T   <p>Be careful not to swap the coordinates of the center point. The center of the circle can be found by taking the average of the x-coordinates and the average of the y-coordinates of the endpoints of the diameter.<\/p>   -  0   -1  prt1-2-F       2   NumDecPlaces  ans1  ta1  2  1  =  1   -1  prt1-3-T     -  0   1  prt1-3-F        prt2  1.0000000  1  1   \/*Node 1: Checks for the correct answer *\/ \/*Node 2: mistake: Failing to square the differences when calculating the Distance *\/ mistake2:sqrt((ta1_1-x_1)+(ta2_1-y_1)); \/*Node 3: mistake: Giving the radius as zero *\/ mistake3: 0; \/*Node 4: mistake: Using the distance between A and B as the radius instead of finding the correct radius*\/ mistake4: (sqrt((ta1_1-x_1)^2+(ta2_1-y_1)^2))*2; \/*Node 5: mistake: Making a sign error in the calculation of the radius.i.e subtracting where addition needs to be done*\/ mistake5:sqrt((ta1_1-x_1)^2-(ta2_1-y_1)^2); \/*Node 6: Checks for the correct answer in decimal form *\/    0   AlgEquiv  ans2  ta2   1  =  1   -1  prt2-1-T     =  0   5  prt2-1-F       1   AlgEquiv  ans2  mistake2   1  +  0   -1  prt2-2-T   <p>You seem to have failed to square the differences when calculating the Distance . Check the worked solution below.<\/p>   -  0   2  prt2-2-F       2   AlgEquiv  ans2  mistake3   1  +  0   -1  prt2-3-T   <p>The radius of a circle cannot be zero; it must be a positive value.Try again <\/p>   -  0   3  prt2-3-F       3   AlgEquiv  ans2  mistake4   1  +  0   -1  prt2-4-T     -  0   4  prt2-4-F       4   AlgEquiv  ans2  mistake5   1  +  0   -1  prt2-5-T   <p>Pay attention to the signs when calculating the radius. Make sure to use the correct mathematical operation (addition or subtraction) based on the formula for finding the distance between two points<\/p>   -  0   -1  prt2-5-F       5   AlgEquiv  ans2  ta2a   0  =  1   -1  prt2-6-T     -  0   1  prt2-6-F       1321285175  2103037030  1565314750  759227565  1450326208  909195231  1747515012  1583556043  1772451748  759722271  1281716420  1280129141  1326846295  2033468365  385591872  266575066  1054284119  376707875  169777034  540566832  1171788230  1808315528  41728822  1652602075  715834249  1642552509  912353214  961756473  1604147240  823250052  858703707  813369643  319857585  1729326571  1527698153  2054331051  1760820871  2131347061  1808942032  3191122  2075727468  88737193  1282669723  605197555  1608556749  1394952115  2121034664  2127920526  979262539  1411756166  756732779  2146018533  1278410301  1590974849  1866921853  1041816146  239709188  236644114  659010716  606359946  1240390795  733577585  2058760331  2093645051  327706133  350894876  1622698800  1597418413  1686342862  1125133157  1646449321  95936243  1351947844  1790680661  72005198  1478232569  1141525198  796244346  846850403  1400068983  1466047133  1097072540  1539133990  397637067  769431130  1272646635  458963379  1706188228  664919709  463579430  1064784690  1744263874  1046440830  664108883  1488185267  1941187704  1693514136  435164003  682276301  1334044098   1    ans1  ta1    ans2  ta2    prt1  1.0000000  0.0000000  prt1-1-T    prt2  1.0000000  0.0000000  prt2-1-T        Add review   "
