  "id": "subsec-intersection-of-a-circle-with-14",
  "level": "2",
  "url": "sec-circles.html#subsec-intersection-of-a-circle-with-14",
  "type": "Checkpoint",
  "number": "4.2.17",
  "title": "",
  "body": "     Tangent Line and Circle with x-axis Center    <p>Suppose the line \\( y = {@slope*x@} \\) is tangent to a circle at point \\( P({@p_x@},{@p_y@}) \\). <br>If the center of the circle is on the \\(x\\)-axis, then find the following.<\/p> <br> <p>(a) The center of the circle:<\/p> <p> Center: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]<\/p> <p>[[feedback:prt1]]<\/p> <br> <p>(b) The radius of the circle:<\/p> <p>Radius: [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]<\/p> <p>[[feedback:prt2]]<\/p> <br> <p>(b) The equation of the circle:<\/p> <p>Equation: [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]<\/p> <p>[[feedback:prt3]]<\/p>    <h3>Worked Solution<\/h3> <p> Let the center of the circle be \\(C(h,0)\\). We need to find the value of \\(h\\). <br>Since the line \\( y={@slope*x@} \\) is tangent to the circle at point \\( P({@p_x@},{@p_y@}) \\), the tangent line is perpendicular to the radius at point \\(P\\). <br>This means the slope of line \\(CP\\) is the negative reciprocal of the slope of \\( y={@slope@} x \\).<\/p> <br> <p>The slope of the line \\( y= {@slope*x@} \\) is \\({@slope@}\\). Therefore, the slope of line \\(CP\\) is \\({@slope1@} \\).<\/p> <p>Using the slope formula: <\/p> <p style=\"margin-left:30px\">The slope of \\( CP = \\frac{{@p_y@} - 0}{{@p_x@} - h }= {@slope1@} \\).<\/p> <p>Solve for \\(h\\):<\/p> <p style=\"margin-left:30px\">\\(\\frac{{@p_y@}}{{@p_x@} - h }= {@slope1@}\\)<\/p> <p style=\"margin-left:30px\">\\({@p_y@}= {@(p_x - h)*(slope1)@}\\)<\/p> <p style=\"margin-left:30px\">\\(h ={@-((p_y\/(slope1) )-p_x)@}\\)<\/p> <p>So, the center of the circle is \\(C({@h_val@},0)\\).<\/p> <br> <p>The distance between the center \\(C\\) and point \\(P\\) is the radius \\(r\\) of the circle. <br>Using the distance formula:<\/p> <p style=\"margin-left:30px\">\\(\\begin{align} \\displaystyle r & = \\sqrt{(x_1-h)^2+(y_1-k)^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{({@p_x@} {@if c_x<0 then \"+\" else \"-\" @} {@abs(c_x)@})^2 + ({@p_y@} - {@c_y@})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{({@p_x-c_x@})^2 + ({@p_y -c_y@})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{{@(p_x-c_x)^2 + (p_y -c_y)^2@}} \\\\ &={@sqrt((p_x-c_x)^2 + (p_y -c_y)^2)@} \\end{align}\\)<\/p> <p>Now we have the center \\(C({@c_x@},{@c_y@})\\) and the radius \\(r = {@ta2@}\\).<\/p> <br> <p>The equation of a circle centered at \\((h,k)\\) with radius \\(r\\) is given by:<\/p> <p style=\"margin-left:30px\">\\( (x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2 \\)<\/p> <p>Plugging in the values we found, gives the equation of the circle:<\/p> <p style=\"margin-left:30px\">\\((x {@if c_x<0 then \"+\" else \"-\" @} {@abs(c_x)@})^2 + y^2 = {@ta2^2@}\\)<\/p>   1  0.1  0    2023060500    \/*Question Variables*\/ slope:rand_with_prohib(-2,2,[0]); p_x:rand_with_prohib(-2,2,[0]); p_y:slope*p_x; slope1:-1\/slope; c_x:-((p_y\/slope1)-p_x); c_y:0; h_val:c_x; ta1:[h_val,0]; ta2:ratsimp(sqrt((p_x-h_val)^2+(p_y-0)^2)); ta3:(x-h_val)^2+(y-0)^2=ta2^2;       <p>The line \\( y = {@slope*x@} \\) is tangent to a circle at point \\( P({@p_x@},{@p_y@}) \\)<\/p> <p>Center: \\({@ta1@}\\)<\/p> <p>Radius: \\({@ta2@}\\)<\/p> <p>Equation: \\({@ta3@}\\)<\/p>      1  0  0   <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:green;\"><i class=\"fa fa-check\"><\/i><\/span> Correct answer, well done.    <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:orange;\"><i class=\"fa fa-adjust\"><\/i><\/span> Your answer is partially correct.    <span style=\"font-size: 1.5em; color:red;\"><i class=\"fa fa-times\"><\/i><\/span> Incorrect answer.   .  *10  none  1  i  cos-1  lang  [  0    ans1  algebraic  ta1  10  1  0  [?,?]  0    1  0  0  1  3     ans2  algebraic  ta2  10  1  0   0    1  0  0  1  3     ans3  algebraic  ta3  15  1  0   0    1  0  0  1  3     prt1  1.0000000  1  1   \/* Node 1: Check for the correct answer *\/    0   AlgEquiv  ans1  ta1   0  =  1   -1  prt1-1-T     =  0   -1  prt1-1-F        prt2  1.0000000  1  1   \/* Node 1: Check for the correct answer *\/    0   AlgEquiv  ans2  ta2   0  =  1   -1  prt2-1-T     =  0   -1  prt2-1-F        prt3  1.0000000  1  1   \/* Node 1: Check for the correct answer *\/    0   AlgEquiv  ans3  ta3   0  =  1   -1  prt3-1-T     =  0   -1  prt3-1-F       1097653564  1961864816  1859365702  2058867260  1254668605  67360108  1357067007  1336609810  884489855  183943631  1436773572  1393330079  1068237912   1    ans1  ta1    ans2  ta2    ans3  ta3    prt1  1.0000000  0.0000000  prt1-1-T    prt2  1.0000000  0.0000000  prt2-1-T    prt3  1.0000000  0.0000000  prt3-1-T        Add review   "
